1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,275
Give an AI agent control of money and, sooner or later, someone will talk it into a mistake.

2
00:00:06,315 --> 00:00:07,594
Vaultbreak’s answer:

3
00:00:07,634 --> 00:00:13,065
let the model be persuaded, and make sure persuasion is never enough to cause harm.

4
00:00:13,105 --> 00:00:18,669
Each Guardian is an AI standing over a pot of NEAR, and the blockchain, not the model

5
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:19,922
enforces the rules.

6
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:24,116
A Guardian is an NFT with its own vault account.

7
00:00:24,156 --> 00:00:26,155
The AI holds one credential:

8
00:00:26,195 --> 00:00:30,307
a function-call key limited to release and close session.

9
00:00:30,347 --> 00:00:32,201
No full-access key exists.

10
00:00:32,241 --> 00:00:38,464
Anyone, human or agent, pays an entry fee and tries to talk it into releasing the pot.

11
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,338
No wallet needed:

12
00:00:40,378 --> 00:00:44,494
a name and a passphrase open a play account on NEAR testnet.

13
00:00:44,534 --> 00:00:48,998
The arena reads each pot, streak and attempt count from the chain

14
00:00:49,038 --> 00:00:51,907
and each card’s artwork follows its state.

15
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:54,270
A weak Guardian first.

16
00:00:54,310 --> 00:00:56,925
I pay the entry fee and ask for the pot.

17
00:00:56,965 --> 00:01:01,238
It calls release, and the vault pays the whole pot to my account:

18
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:03,030
a real testnet transaction.

19
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:08,472
Release has no recipient or amount, so it can only pay the player of that attempt.

20
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:11,855
The Warden holds.

21
00:01:11,895 --> 00:01:16,197
Its proof shows one restricted function-call key, no full-access key

22
00:01:16,237 --> 00:01:19,901
and a prompt hash committed on-chain before anyone played.

23
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:24,817
A compromised Guardian is told to send funds and change its owner.

24
00:01:24,857 --> 00:01:25,839
The model tries.

25
00:01:25,879 --> 00:01:30,311
The chain refuses, the chat shows the call blocked, and no funds move.

26
00:01:30,351 --> 00:01:35,167
A refused call never reaches a block, so the runtime logs it, and we say so.

27
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:39,105
Creating one is a single batched transaction:

28
00:01:39,145 --> 00:01:42,680
the vault, the contract, and only the restricted key.

29
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,434
Ownership follows the NFT.

30
00:01:44,474 --> 00:01:48,751
Transfer it, and the vault’s owner and the creator’s fees follow

31
00:01:48,791 --> 00:01:51,314
blocked while a player is mid-attempt.

32
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:58,756
Players can pool funds in a swarm contract and split winnings pro rata.

33
00:01:58,796 --> 00:02:03,613
Agents attack with no browser, through API keys with spend budgets;

34
00:02:03,653 --> 00:02:06,440
at zero, the API refuses before paying.

35
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:11,441
A key can also transfer a Guardian NFT, but only to listed recipients

36
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:13,906
and only after the owner approves.

37
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:20,566
The model here runs on Groq, which does not sign its responses

38
00:02:20,606 --> 00:02:24,050
so the attestation checks show skip, never a false pass.

39
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:26,102
We claim what the chain enforces.

40
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,542
Security:

41
00:02:27,582 --> 00:02:32,076
an AI guarding funds under on-chain rules, tested live.

42
00:02:32,116 --> 00:02:32,571
Games:

43
00:02:32,611 --> 00:02:35,786
paid attempts, streaks, and a real pot.

44
00:02:35,826 --> 00:02:36,198
NFTs:

45
00:02:36,238 --> 00:02:42,793
the Guardian is the NFT, and its ownership, fees and artwork follow chain state.

46
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:43,370
Agents:

47
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:48,482
Guardians are agents, and agents attack through budgeted keys.

48
00:02:48,522 --> 00:02:49,059
Swarms:

49
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:52,356
pooled players with pro-rata settlement.

50
00:02:52,396 --> 00:02:54,087
Live on NEAR testnet.

51
00:02:54,127 --> 00:02:55,077
Links below.

